a_question:
Let \((a_n)\) and \((b_n)\) be sequences of non‑negative real numbers with \(a_n \le b_n\) for every \(n\in\mathbb{N}\). Using the fact that a series of non‑negative terms converges if and only if its sequence of partial sums is bounded, prove that:

(i) if \(\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} b_n\) converges then \(\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} a_n\) converges;

(ii) if \(\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} a_n\) diverges then \(\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} b_n\) diverges.

